 To solve the system of linear equations using Cramer's rule, we first need to find the determinant of the coefficient matrix, which we'll call D. The coefficient matrix is:

$$
\begin{bmatrix}
2 & 3 & 1 \\
4 & 4 & 4 \\
1 & 1 & 8
\end{bmatrix}
$$

The determinant D is:

$$
D = 2 \cdot (4 \cdot 8 - 4 \cdot 1) - 3 \cdot (1 \cdot 8 - 4 \cdot 1) + 1 \cdot (4 \cdot 1 - 1 \cdot 4)
$$

$$
D = 2 \cdot (32 - 4) - 3 \cdot (8 - 4) + 1 \cdot (4 - 4)
$$

$$
D = 2 \cdot 28 - 3 \cdot 4 + 1 \cdot 0
$$

$$
D = 56 - 12
$$

$$
D = 44
$$

Now, we'll find the determinants for the systems with each variable replaced by a column vector. Let's replace the first variable x with a column vector [x; y; z]:

$$
\begin{bmatrix}
y & 1 & z \\
